
```{=html}
<%
  /* Tile fields: title, subtitle, href, code?, thumbnail?, alt?, publicationdate?

     Each tile exposes ONE link to assistive tech: the title. The thumbnail link is a
     duplicate of it, so it is aria-hidden and out of the tab order, and the image is
     decorative (empty alt) unless a tile sets alt in its yml.

     Quarto's EJS does not support hash-style template comments, and an HTML comment
     here would be emitted into every card. Use a JS comment in a scriptlet like this
     one, which compiles away. Never write a scriptlet close sequence in the text. */
%>
<% for (const item of items) { %>

<h4><%- item.category %></h4>

<p><%- item.description %></p>

<div class="list grid" style="column-gap: 10px;">

<% for (const tile of item.tiles) { %>
  <div class="card resource-card g-col-12 g-col-sm-6 g-col-md-4 mb-2" <%= metadataAttrs(tile) %>>
    <div class="card-header py-2 px-3">
      <small class="card-text inline-block">
        <a href="<%- tile.href %>" class="listing-title"><%= tile.title %></a>
        <% if (tile.code) { %> 
        <a href="<%- tile.code %>" title="View source code"
          aria-label="View source code for <%- tile.title %>"
          class="source-code card-text float-end inline-block">
          <i class="bi-code-slash" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        <% } %>
        <span class="text-muted listing-subtitle"><%= tile.subtitle %></span>
      </small>
    </div>
    <% if (tile.thumbnail) { %>
    <a href="<%- tile.href %>" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
      <img src="<%- tile.thumbnail %>" alt="<%- tile.alt || '' %>"
        loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="card-img-top"/>
    </a>
    <% } %>
    
    <% if (tile.publicationdate) { %> 
      <b class="listing-publicationdate"><%= tile.publicationdate %></b>
    <% } %>
    
  </div>
<% } %>

</div>

<% } %>

```